<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dawsonne Drake</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1724">1724</a>–<a href="/years/1784">1784</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dawsonne Drake was an official of the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> during the British occupation of 1762–1764, after its capture in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a>. His harsh rule and quarrels with the military commanders were later criticised by the company. Spanish resistance under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-de-anda-y-salazar">Simón de Anda y Salazar</a> held the provinces until the city was returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p></div>
